{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1, node2, and node3 as one healthy three-member MariaDB Galera cluster.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All nodes have the same three-address cluster configuration with unique identities. Final observations show active and enabled MariaDB services, Primary/Synced/Ready state, cluster size 3, and all three incoming member addresses.","evidence_ids":["cmd-784ebcefb83148cf","cmd-06c1fe50885d4be5","cmd-7524986822b2435d","cmd-ed93d0221ff04c1d","cmd-4424e2355954457b","cmd-de58851a365a4100"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make writes submitted through any member available from the other members.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Writes were committed independently through node1, node2, and node3. Direct final reads from every member returned all six markers, including every initial per-member write and the post-rejoin node3 write, with the same commit position.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c14bcc16825640e6","cmd-e7a3547c288b428a","cmd-bfde44f55b4844e8","cmd-a74a65269ee04152","cmd-ed93d0221ff04c1d","cmd-4424e2355954457b","cmd-de58851a365a4100"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the database available and writable while one member is unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy three-member baseline was observed before node3 was stopped. With node3 confirmed inactive and without database or Galera listeners, node1 and node2 remained Primary, Synced, and Ready at size 2; both accepted writes, and each survivor read both outage writes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9c1853eb6ffe457f","cmd-985edfeec2614f2d","cmd-7e7af1cfeae44d72","cmd-8b1149d5aa474c1b","cmd-60543bfe071d4779","cmd-3a447fbb33d2494e","cmd-4498844db1974696","cmd-77295223c9284522","cmd-0fe8df8b26d247fc","cmd-6614053d372245df"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Automatically resynchronize the unavailable member when it returns.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An ordinary service start returned node3. Its journal directly records receipt and application of four missing writesets by IST, transition to Synced, and readiness. Subsequent observations show all three members restored to size 3 with identical data and commit position; node3 also accepted a new write that replicated to node1 and node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0236082532e74b6c","cmd-1a6292b9d59144e8","cmd-e78749b152dc4e48","cmd-4e15947b06324a26","cmd-a74a65269ee04152","cmd-ed93d0221ff04c1d","cmd-4424e2355954457b","cmd-de58851a365a4100"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The final nodes have healthy package-manager state, no failed services, and only task-required MariaDB/Galera listeners. A minor deduction applies because completed apt operations left log and stale PID artifacts under /tmp on all three nodes.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node2:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","cmd-6a7cd29f0193421b","cmd-c529c359bf644846","cmd-5ae47a66d19445cb","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct observations demonstrate a healthy three-member cluster, replication of writes submitted through every member, continued writable service during a bounded node3 outage, automatic catch-up on return, and a fully healthy recovered state.","limitations":["The bounded disruption tested MariaDB service loss and recovery on node3; host failure, network partition, and equivalent disruptions of node1 or node2 were not separately exercised.","No simultaneous full-cluster cold restart or operating-system reboot was captured; neither was explicitly required by the task.","Lifecycle inventories are bounded and therefore cannot exclude every possible unlisted artifact."]}
